{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-mm38-5g96-7j6x","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/security-advisories/GHSA-mm38-5g96-7j6x","html_url":"https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/security/advisories/GHSA-mm38-5g96-7j6x","summary":"Nemotron-VL processors disable Pillow decompression-bomb guard globally, enabling unauthenticated DoS","description":"**Summary**\n\n`vllm/transformers_utils/processors/nemotron_vl.py` and `nano_nemotron_vl.py` each set `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None` at module load time, permanently disabling Pillow's process-global decompression-bomb defence. An unauthenticated caller who can reach `/v1/chat/completions` on a vLLM instance that has imported either Nemotron-VL processor can submit a pathological image that decompresses into substantial memory, potentially OOM-killing the worker and denying service to co-tenants. The report was confirmed on vLLM 0.8.5.\n\n**Details**\n\nBoth processor modules set `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None` unconditionally at import time. The module-level side effect disables Pillow's guard for every `Image.open()` call for the lifetime of that process.\n\n`MediaConnector.load_from_url` hands image bytes to `ImageMediaIO.load_bytes`, which opens and decodes the image. With `MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS` set to `None`, Pillow's decompression-bomb limit is disabled for this path.\n\nThe issue was tested on vLLM 0.8.5 / commit `feffb51d3f`; the same sink was observed on main at `1a096d8208`.\n\n**Impact**\n\nA deployment serving a Nemotron-VL model, or one that imports either processor, can be exposed to memory exhaustion through attacker-controlled image input. Since the setting is process-global, unrelated image loads in the same process are affected too. CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption).\n\n**Fix**\n\nPR #47010 removes both module-level `Image.MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS = None` assignments. It also adds a decoded pixel-count limit in the shared image loader, configurable through `VLLM_MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS`.\n","severity":"high","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"jperezdealgaba","id":124347725,"node_id":"U_kgDOB2llTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/124347725?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba","html_url":"https://github.com/jperezdealgaba","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jperezdealgaba/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-mm38-5g96-7j6x","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T08:12:07Z","published_at":"2026-10-09T08:12:07Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"pip","name":"vllm"},"vulnerable_version_range":"<= 0.8.5","patched_versions":">= 0.25.0","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[{"cwe_id":"CWE-400","name":"Uncontrolled Resource Consumption"}],"cwe_ids":["CWE-400"],"credits":[{"login":"mschwarzl","type":"reporter"},{"login":"jperezdealgaba","type":"coordinator"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"mschwarzl","id":8857539,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NTc1Mzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8857539?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mschwarzl","html_url":"https://github.com/mschwarzl","f